// The two floating-point types, made on first use rather than with the standard
// ones: every node made at start-up moves the ids of everything parsed after it,
// and a program without floating point has no need of them. fltys[0] is 1 once
// they exist, fltys[1] the double and fltys[2] the float.
fl_types() {
  int made = (import fltys)[0];
  if(made == 0) {
    fl_make();
  }
} return void;
